## Registry sync (same change)

When adding or changing steward CLI in a step file, update the node in `.cursor/foundry/flows/factory-flow.yaml`:

| Step adds… | Update in YAML |
|---|---|
| `visit state patch` | `allow.cli`: `visit.state_patch`; `allow.state`: patched paths |
| `ledger show` | `allow.cli`: `ledger.show` |
| `artifact publish` | `allow.cli`: `artifact.publish`; `produces` + `allow.files.write` |
| `receipt seal` | `allow.cli`: `receipt.link`; `receipts` schemas |
| `visit transition` | `allow.cli`: `transition` |
| Receipt/artifact draft paths | `allow.files.write` for each path written before seal |

Do **not** add `allow.cli` for engine hooks (`app validate`, catalog checks) or product bootstrap (`run create`, `run context --markdown`, `cli resolve`).

Do **not** change `instructions:` unless deliberately rebinding a different step file.

When `allow.cli` changes, update acceptance features under `.cursor/foundry/cli/tests/acceptance/features/` and run `foundry dev acceptance`.

## Engine domain — keep out of step files

Lifecycle states, hook names, catalog check ids, connection selection, admission source, and links to node reference docs.

Steward **may** read ledger events when assembling **intake-receipt** evidence — that is not re-running hooks. Agent-receipt step instructions do not include `ledger show`.

## Anti-patterns

| Anti-pattern | Fix |
|---|---|
| "Contract in factory-flow.yaml" header | Delete |
| Steward drafts ticket then re-drafts from worker | Worker proposes; steward writes once |
| ` ```text ` / shell fences for foundry argv | `foundry-invoke` |
| Hook names in steward text | On intake nodes: "ledger `check.recorded` for this visit" |
| `ledger show --visit` | Filter by `visit_id` in assembly |
| Inlined receipt JSON field recipes | "Build draft per `registry:schemas/…`" |
| Catalog check ids in Boundaries | Plain-language prohibition |
| Step > 80 lines | Trim; reference schemas |
| Steward CLI without `allow.cli` update | Registry sync in same change |
| Separate `instructions_path` read after markdown packet | Follow inlined `## Instructions` |

## Before merge

- [ ] ≤ 80 lines; `foundry-invoke` fences; packet placeholders
- [ ] Goal has no routing target; boundaries have no catalog check ids
- [ ] Evidence order and branch CLI fences complete
- [ ] `allow.cli` / `allow.state` / `allow.files.write` match the step
- [ ] `foundry dev acceptance` passes
